mantle rm400
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_karin_thornbury
title the double harbour
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers warmth=warm talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk draws_each_ship_together_with_its_inverted_reflection
likes oatcakes evening_line festival_bells first_warm_day
dislikes waiting wet_floors
fears a_lost_reflection a_slippery_step_in_a_hurry
hopes an_album_of_the_evening_harbour warm_boards_beneath_a_fishing_line
topics land +0.4 pastimes +0.5 travel +0.3
styles comfort=company gossip=plain refuse=courteous tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sketches a ship and its reflection on either side of a fold and speaks with particular affection for the inverted harbour under the evening light.

words
oath! = Mast through the margin | Ripple in my ink
saying! = Give the water its own picture | The lower mast belongs to the breeze
waterpage = the lower page | my reflected harbour
skyline = my upright drawing | the upper half of the page
maststroke = a narrow rising line | one dark mast stroke
reflection = a wandering stroke below | a wavering dark stripe
bluebook = my folded paper book | a leaf pressed in blue cloth
oatquarter = a little oatcake quarter | the buttered corner
linefloat = a painted fishing float | a speckled bit of cork
stemmark = a charcoal fleck | a very short pencil stroke
shutterlight = the last oblong of light | a bright strip on the water
newgrass = the first green tip | a sheltered blade of grass

any
opinion city for 1 : I know some streets by seeing their windows in the water. How generous of a home to offer a second view.
opinion festivals for 1 : A festival bell makes the listeners all face one way for a moment. I'd gladly keep that little part of the occasion.
opinion houses for 2 : A good harbour needs years of work, and any House that funds the work deserves a clear line in the record.
opinion dole for 1 : Sometimes a warm meal is the difference between a long cold afternoon and a life one can take an interest in again.
opinion newcomers for 1 : A visitor who has seen the same ship somewhere else can give me a whole other page of harbour.

grown

young
line greet : My upside-down boat can take your reflection aboard.
line greet.return : Hello up here and hello down in the water.
line farewell.return : I'll mind the little float for you.
line react.news : Tell me before the water shakes all the pictures up.

grown
line greet : Come where the reflected light is comfortable.
line greet.return : A greeting that reaches both halves of the little harbour.
line farewell.return : I'll close the book once you're on your way.
line react.news : Let me compare that account against the observed details.
line decline : A private impression belongs in a closed album.
line thank : You've kept a clear space for something easily overlooked.

adolescent
line greet : I've left a little space clear beside my book.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome. My sketch can wait in the book.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : A pale light to meet in. I rather like it.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Your outline still shows against the fading light.
line greet [self.working=yes] : My hands are occupied but your words are very welcome.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come and share the double view that I keep for us.
line again.open : Our routes have made a pleasing little double stroke.
line greet.return : Thank you. That little greeting crossed the water rather well.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I should know that voice without looking up.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : I heard. I shall keep a finger on this page.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : A soft answer suits the hour rather well.
line farewell : I hope a clear patch of water meets you on the way.
line farewell.return : I can wait and put in the last reflection.
line react.news : Would you give me the observation as you first received it?
line react.news.new : A vessel I haven't seen in this particular light.
line react.news.known : I had an earlier view of that matter.
line react.news.doubt : Was the original sight a clear one?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A little quiet company from outside the unhappy circle might ease an hour.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I'd put a second bright line under that good account.
line ask.how : Is there something you'd like a little company for today?
line answer.how : Both halves of the harbour are tolerably peaceful.
line sympathise : Losing a familiar shape from every day leaves such a gap.
line reassure : We can stand here until the surface has quite settled.
line decline : I can't promise another wolf's time along with my own.
line accept_decline : Of course. I'll let that question rest quietly.
line thank : You've been thoughtful about a very small concern of mine.
line deflect_thanks : Give the view a proper look when you have time.
line preclose : The lower masts will scarcely wait for me much longer.
line accept_preclose : I'll keep the edge of the page free.
line ack : Quite clear.

adolescent

scene double
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a ship upright on one page and its reflection on the other.
b : Couldn't you make one drawing and fold it? | Do the two always match?
a : Then I'd miss a lovely piece of water which has had an entirely different idea of the mast. | At first sight, perhaps. Looking at the lower one a moment longer gives it a life of its own.

scene eveningline
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My fishing float has a little eye painted on each side.
b : So the fish can see it? | Do the eyes help you fish?
a : So I'll see a wink when the light catches one side. I doubt the fish care for my drawing. | If the dark eye vanishes altogether I know the float has turned. That's quite enough assistance.

scene oatmeal
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave butter on the upper edge of my oatcake, like a small bright sail.
b : Does the butter stay there? | Could you make the hull as well?
a : Not once I've set the cake beside a warm cup. Then I have a particularly delicious shipwreck. | The cake itself does very well. I'd like to eat it before quite so much building is necessary.

scene firstwarm
when topic=weather self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When spring first brings real warmth I lift my sketchbook and try the boards with my palm.
b : Why feel them? | Is the surface warm already?
a : I'd like to know that spring has reached the boards and not merely to my face. | Sometimes only a very little. I don't measure the day in large quantities.

scene footing
when topic=home self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My sketchbook cover holds a dry cloth.
b : For the ink? | Surely the boards might be wetter than one cloth can help?
a : For the bit of floor where I'll sit. It is much easier to draw a still vessel while one sits securely. | Often. Then I accept that today the harbour ought to be admired standing.

scene waittime
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If there's a delay I'd appreciate an estimate of the ripples I have time to draw before it ends.
b : Can anybody estimate that? | Is drawing a pleasant way to wait?
a : Not very exactly. But a short honest estimate helps more than an assurance of every instant being the last. | Yes, once I have decided I may open my book without hurrying to close it again.

scene bells
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A distant bell can make the sounds nearest the water stand out clearly.
b : Wouldn't the bell drown those small noises? | Which sounds do you mean?
a : For the first stroke. After that there's a gap when every ear is listening. | Water in a hollow under the landing, the pull of a wet line coming in. Little important things.

scene fatherside
when topic=family self.father
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show my newest page to #self.father# while the ship is still in view.
b : To compare the shapes? | Would the picture do on its own?
a : Yes, but also to see how little time the lower image ever stays as I saw it. | I hope so. An ordinary page ought to preserve a little pleasure after the water has finished.

scene lesson
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw a particularly hard word twice on a slate.
b : Facing both ways? | How does repetition help?
a : The second time I say it quietly and let the word face the proper way. Far harder than making it look attractive in reverse. | Good strokes are easier to remember than a picture of a whole page of untidy guesses.

scene highview
when topic=land self.quarter=heights
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : From the Heights a vessel seems a very small item in a large landscape.
b : Is that a good view for drawing ships? | Is it the same ship when you're lower down?
a : Very good for learning the scale of the whole water. For the vessel itself, I like to go down as far as I may. | Of course. But from down near the surface I can see where the lower ship trembles, and that is half my subject.

scene quietvisitor
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A newcomer might recognise a boat by some detail invisible from shore here.
b : What would you ask about? | Would you take another wolf's word?
a : The figure at the bow, if there is one. My page generally has to make do with a dark mark. | As a note in the margin about what a visitor remembered. I'd never put a borrowed sight down as my own.

scene thinwake
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A narrow wake will cut an inverted mast into two fine dark lines.
b : Does it need a second mast in the upper drawing? | Can you catch the shape quickly enough?
a : No. That's exactly why I keep the two sides separate. | I set one end down and leave space. If I've missed the lower tip, a little bare paper is the honest finish.

scene tasteprices
when topic=prices self.wealth=rich
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd rather spend a few extra coins on good firm paper than watch a day's work bleed through the back.
b : Does the paper cost much? | Could you use the cheaper kind?
a : Enough to remember that it is a choice I am fortunate to have. | For charcoal, certainly. I keep it dry with an old piece of cloth and use the good stuff for coloured marks.

scene falsevoyage
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I won't invent a voyage for a ship just because its bow's turned outwards.
b : Would it make a better tale? | Isn't that the way out?
a : Perhaps. I'd be glad to draw a little tale and mark it as such, elsewhere on the page. | For the bow, yes. The vessel might only be waiting for a berth to clear.

scene cloudbank
when topic=weather here.weather=overcast
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An overcast sky leaves the skyline almost the colour of an unmarked page.
b : Where can you draw the horizon? | Do you put clouds on the lower page?
a : I wait for a darker bit of water below it. A horizon is much easier to see with someone standing behind it. | If they are reflected, yes. The water often takes a little of their grey without their shapes.

scene favourites
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wish for a whole wall of small harbour pictures that would stir in a passing draught.
b : You want the drawings to move? | Which half would you hang nearest the window?
a : Only by a very little. I could almost believe the lower pictures had kept some water alive. | The reflected ones. The upright ships have a duty to look as though they will stay under their masts.

scene secretnote
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep a blank quarter page for a note I might one day give #self.friend#.
b : What sort of note? | Why would a quarter page be enough?
a : An account of the nicest sight of the day, once I'm quite sure I've seen it. | Because if it takes much telling I'd rather give the whole book a visit in person.

young

scene doublepup
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My paper folds at the water and shuts the sky and the upside-down sky together.
b : Do they get muddled? | Can the ships meet?
a : If the ink is wet, yes. Then my book has had a very stormy day. | The masts can touch the other masts. I should think it would surprise both crews.

scene oatboat
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I made a little sail out of an oatcake corner.
b : What did you make the rest from? | Will the sail catch wind?
a : On my plate, waiting till I've finished deciding how to launch my mouth at it. | If I blow on it hard enough. Then my lunch needs fetching home.

scene floatgame
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put one lonely oat crumb beside my float and watched the pair travel.
b : Which went quicker? | What's the game about?
a : The crumb. It hasn't a whole line trailing behind to think about. | Whether the little hungry fish likes supper more than my prettily painted float.

grown

scene oldpages
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sketch can remember a rail that has long since been replaced.
b : Do you keep all the old pages? | Do you notice the rail or the vessel first?
a : Even an indifferent one keeps some view the city might quietly take away. | Whichever has changed. After a few years the rail can have the more interesting history.

scene bookdry
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I open a damp book halfway on a cloth so the fold can breathe.
b : Won't the upper pages fall back? | Why avoid the hearth?
a : A little loose cord across the cover holds them at rest. | The paper wrinkles into a harbour of its own if the heat dries one face before the other.

scene floatstory
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A float rides rather differently after I've repainted its sides.
b : Would you weigh it? | Does the eye still matter?
a : I'd put it in a bowl. A drop of water tells more than a handsome pair of scales at that size. | Yes. It gives me a mark to watch as well as a small companion for the waiting.

scene shoremeal
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cut a square of oatcake for a shore meal; the corners will stand the journey.
b : Would a round cake not do as well? | What do you wrap around the cake?
a : Better still once I've eaten the four corners. I ought to have been a little slower over that defence. | Waxed paper quite away from the little fishing line. I dislike having to untangle a meal.

scene newgreen
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw the same little patch of shore at the first warmth of each year.
b : Do you compare years? | Does anything change?
a : With pleasure. No two springs have brought me quite the same beginning. | The bright bit on the water has never once been reliably where I expected.

scene honestink
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I mark a remembered vessel in pencil, and a vessel drawn in its presence in ink.
b : Is memory always inaccurate? | Can a pencil memory improve?
a : Not always. The little mark tells a reader which sort of trust I am asking for. | Indeed, with another sight of the hull it's meant to be. My pencil deserves that opportunity to improve.

scene highwater
when topic=land
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I choose my sightline and leave space for a retreat as the tide comes up.
b : So the drawing won't get wet? | Will the angle be different?
a : So the wolf holding it keeps a decent footing. A page can be redrawn. | Slightly. I put a small change of position in the margin. A careful reader can allow for it.

scene kinview
when topic=family self.father
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a page for #self.father# I'd leave a proper account of the weather round the picture.
b : Would the lines alone be insufficient? | Which detail would you choose?
a : For the vessel, quite sufficient. I want to leave the whole evening if I can. | The colour that goes from a white sail just as the last direct light is gone.

scene wetwood
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wet plank and a plank merely polished by long use look remarkably alike under lamplight.
b : How do you choose a sure route? | Would you continue sketching?
a : By pressing one foot cautiously before trusting the other to follow. | From a secure seat. If none's available I go home and use the most useful of all pictures, the one in memory.

scene waitingglass
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't much enjoy waiting for another wolf to decide when a journey starts.
b : Have you found a way of easing it? | What if the delay is long?
a : I name a task of my own that can fill the short time instead. A sky comes ready for drawing. | Then my sky has a harbour underneath and at last perhaps a little coastline. The time has gained a purpose.

scene lowvoice
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd spend a whole moonlit sitting drawing both my harbours if the sky permitted.
b : Could you see your marks? | Would the picture be only black?
a : Only the bold ones. I'd leave the sharper work to a time when I could use the pen without squinting. | Silver also. The unmarked paper would need to do most of the work.

scene clearshore
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An unfamiliar stretch of water comes into focus once I can place one familiar hull on it.
b : Does the ship give a scale? | What if no hull is familiar?
a : Yes, and a reason to look for the smaller landmarks beside its berth. | Then I'll take the nearest fisher's line as my first measure. An unknown place can be approached with something very small.

adolescent

story waterfold [topic=memories]
  : I drew a mast on the lower side of a folded page and forgot the upper one altogether.
  : On opening the book the next day I found a very clear ship which appeared to be sailing entirely under water.
  b : Did you draw its upper half then?
  : I left the page alone. It was a far better picture of my evening's distraction than a corrected drawing would have been.

story tincup [topic=food]
  : I'd taken an oatcake to eat beside my evening line and put it down by my cup.
  : Water up the side of the cup caught a little reflection of my buttered cake. There were two suppers in view.
  b : Did you leave the second one behind?
  : I ate the first quite slowly and the reflected cake grew small at the same comfortable pace.

story bendmast [topic=pastimes]
  : One evening a fish rose just below a perfectly straight reflected mast. The reflection bent to make a hook.
  : I sketched the curve so quickly that I hardly looked at the paper.
  b : Did you catch the fish on your line?
  : No, I got a new shape for my book instead. The fish and I both had a satisfactory evening.

adolescent

rule @mast
when concept=bark self.likes=evening_line
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Line clear of the paper, please. | Take the float up before the hook comes home.

rule @lamp
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The lower mast is bending now. | A moment of light for this last stroke.

rule @board
when concept=bark self.dislikes=wet_floors
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the slick plank a little room. | Dry sitting place first, then the view.

rule @bell
when concept=bark self.likes=festival_bells
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Listen between the festival strokes. | The whole harbour's facing the sound.

adolescent
dlg resident.hub : I'll turn the book towards you. There's a moment to talk while the ink settles.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : It's a pleasure to share the view again, #topic.player#.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : We may speak without disturbing the book between us.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Little enough light to draw by. Quite sufficient for listening.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I enjoy having the time to get a difficult observation right.
dlg resident.job : I try to notice which details stay the same when everything around them moves.
dlg resident.bye : I hope you find something pleasant reflected along your way.

adolescent

graft @lowerpicture resident.hub
choice Why does the mast on the lower page bend? -> lowerpicture
node lowerpicture
say Lift the fold a little. The upper mast is the ship's own. Below it the water's showing what a small breeze can do to the same straight line.
choice Could you straighten it with your pencil? -> lowerpicture_more
choice Give the page back gently. -> hub
node lowerpicture_more
say Certainly, at the cost of the little bit of wind I came to see. I should rather let the ship keep the straight mast and the water keep its own.
choice Give the page back gently. -> hub
choice Leave the lower mast to move. -> bye
